# Deny-by-default. This working copy sits on top of real, private research data
# (specimen records, lab notes, credentials in data/config.json). Nothing is
# tracked unless it is explicitly un-ignored below, so a stray `git add -A`
# cannot publish it.
*

# --- application code + docs (the only things that go to GitHub) ---
!.gitignore
!README.md
!SETUP.md
!CLAUDE.md
!install.sh
!start.sh
!launch.sh
!serve.py

!app/
!app/index.html

!seed/
!seed/projects.json

!tools/
!tools/report.py
!tools/make_app.sh

!assets/
!assets/AppIcon.icns

# --- never tracked, restated for anyone reading this file ---
# data/            live workspace, backups, and data/config.json (API key,
#                  email app password) — all local only
# legacy/          the pre-app markdown project files
# reports/         generated weekly reports, built from real data
# triage/          email triage scratch
# *.eml            saved lab email
